<title>LITHUANIA: BOURSE CAPITALISATION DOWN LAST WEEK.</title>
<headline>BOURSE CAPITALISATION DOWN LAST WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the Vilnius</p>
<p>bourse dropped to 5.621 billion litas last week from 5.726</p>
<p>billion litas the previous week, the stock exchange said on</p>
<p>Monday.</p>
<p>There were six trading sessions last week instead of five</p>
<p>because Saturday was a working day.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					     May 05-10   April 28-30</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		   23,276	  10,405</p>
<p>    Executed orders		    1,917	   866</p>
<p>Number of transactions on</p>
<p>    Central market (CM)		1,481	   802</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL	8,807,190     3,736,580</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    block trades (BT)		  218	     32</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	    6,142,850     3,683,140</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week	60,730,670    30,654,173</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week	4,617,647     3,263,860</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	    3,999,550     2,748,150</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	    6,142,850     3,683,149</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T-bills	    14		6</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	  4,807,640     988,440</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
